== 2026-11-20 12:47:55 #1025: the horizon series' truncation at the solvers' u0 = 0.04, Ks = 30, against D. Written before the run.
Why: check A2's u 0.04 line (for information) reads 3.9e-8 in the tangents at k_c 55, D 17.5 (lane_b12n.log), against 9e-15 at D 13
(dd_checkAB_criteria.log). That is the truncation of the perturbation series where block 12 hands to the segment, shared by the float64
and dd builds, so it is a discretization error of every lambda record, not rounding.
Run: ell_ddm.py sshres --us 0.04 (no bar of record; the printed FAIL is against the default bar) on the k_c 55 states at D 14.5, 15, 15.5,
16, 16.5 (l1kc55Fb1025), 17, 18 (l1kc55Fs1025), 19 (l1kc55F1025), each at its lambda_1 record or estimate, and the D 13, k_c 31 state as the reference.
D 17.5 is in lane_b12n.log. sshres fixes Ks = 30, so the Ks dependence is left for a follow-up.
Reading: the D-trend of the worst tangent residual at u0. If it grows by orders from D 13 to 17.5, the lambda records past the D where it
passes ~1e-10 need a Ks or u0 convergence test before they are trusted to the digits quoted; that test (lambda at Ks 40 or u0 0.02 against
Ks 30, u0 0.04) is proposed to the coordinator, not started.
